nup":true,"mode":"auto"},"review":{"blocking_severities":["critical","high"],"command":"env AP_REVIEWER_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5 AP_REVIEWER_EFFORT=low uv run python -B docs/examples/reviewers/claude_review.py","executor":"command","max_findings":50,"require_command_for":[]},"stage":{"max_attempts":5,"max_restarts":5,"timeout_seconds":660},"worktree":{"copy_files":[".env"],"mode":"in_place","root":null,"setup_command":null}},"findings":[{"action":"ask_user","code_owned":false,"detail":"The companion reads `.agentic-preflight.toml` at the pull request's current `base.sha`. `gh run rerun` replays the original pull_request_target event, which includes the workflow file and base from when that run started. If the base's approval mode changed between those two points, the companion can decide whether to re-run from a different policy than the one the re-run will apply. For example, it can skip an `owner_review` run because the base is now in `environment` mode, or re-run an `environment`-mode run and throw away a granted Environment approval.","fix_commit":"2ed73b6a3c5c188dd1eba1cab75d065c359eaa85","id":"F001","line":73,"path":".github/workflows/human-approval-rerun.yml","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"fixed","suggestion":"Read the mode at the base commit the selected policy run used, taken from the run's event payload or the run's own base, or record why the difference is acceptable.","title":"Approval mode is read from the current base SHA, but the re-run replays the original run's base and workflow","unit":"U0001"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"`gh run rerun` can fail for other reasons: a re-run that is already queued from a concurrent companion, a permission error, or a transient API failure. The error message always tells the maintainer to push again because of the 30-day window, which can send them in the wrong direction.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F002","line":125,"path":".github/workflows/human-approval-rerun.yml","response_note":"Commit 2ed73b6 replaced the blanket 30-day message with GitHub's own error plus the two known causes; the CLI requires one repair commit per finding, and that commit was recorded for F001.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"accepted","suggestion":"Print gh's stderr and word the 30-day limit as one possible cause, not the cause.","title":"Any re-run failure is reported as the 30-day re-run limit","unit":"U0001"},{"action":"ask_user","code_owned":false,"detail":"The companion reads the approval mode only after the policy run completes. A run in `environment` mode stays in progress while its Environment approval is pending, and that can last much longer than 10 minutes. In that case the wait loop runs out and the companion exits 1 with `::error::... Re-run it after it completes so the review is counted`. That run is one the companion would have left alone anyway, and the message tells the user to re-run a run whose re-run would throw away the Environment approval. The result is a red companion run with misleading advice in a mode that does not read reviews.","fix_commit":"f46cdc87491162b86585ee3966927526e054732b","id":"F003","line":85,"path":".github/workflows/human-approval-rerun.yml","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"fixed","suggestion":"Decide whether a run that is still waiting should be checked for its mode first, for example by looking for a pending deployment or a waiting `environment` job through the API. Another option is to exit 0 with a notice when the wait runs out, rather than failing and asking for a re-run.","title":"Companion fails with an error when a review arrives while an environment-mode policy run is waiting for deployment approval","unit":"U0001"},{"action":"auto_fix","code_owned":false,"detail":"The step can wait twice. First it polls for the policy artifact for up to 10 minutes: 60 polls with a 10-second sleep, plus the time each download takes. Then, in review mode, it polls the run status for up to another 10 minutes, plus the time each API call takes. If both waits run to their limit, the total is more than the job's `timeout-minutes: 20`. GitHub then cancels the job before it prints the 'did not finish within 10 minutes' error or the hand re-run guidance, so the user sees a timed-out job with no explanation.","fix_commit":"39ee810d0a0cf7306f7ccf79dc509f7d6718921a","id":"F004","line":35,"path":".github/workflows/human-approval-rerun.yml","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"fixed","suggestion":"Make the job timeout longer than the combined waits (for example 25 minutes), or share one deadline between the two loops.","title":"The job's 20-minute timeout can end the run before the companion explains why it stopped","unit":"U0001"}],"fingerprint":{"base_tree_sha":"8781de91bef2081f62309dc01bb8f4a0b81a13ad","config_sha256":"64ebd95cb7eea63aa3314d30f8066a3b3fc1290f8222e60e9235d3cc1cbaecc9","configuration_supported":true,"diff_sha256":"0e794f21324f340618c43233ab16c5d5f0e5dc8ab1815b10b7b9ba8210a5b7f3","excluded_files":[],"executor":"command","grounding_sha256":"6937df508eedfa38e783092ad97e02b3812b1e0d711005009cfe2b793d1dac0b","head_tree_sha":"a9085b0173fed1bfb095a9524aef211405cd0756","intent_sha256":"1125d2d4c8db48e563cf282396eabdf72d82bd2bc9743963365dc1f02dca0ed0","version":2},"finished_at":"2026-11-02T05:08:46Z","head_sha":"39ee810d0a0cf7306f7ccf79dc509f7d6718921a","result":{"command":"env AP_REVIEWER_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5 AP_REVIEWER_EFFORT=low uv run python -B docs/examples/reviewers/claude_review.py","coverage":{"cited_units":[],"clean_units":["U0001","U0002","U0003","U0004","U0005","U0006","U0007","U0008","U0009","U0010","U0011","U0012","U0013","U0014","U0015","U0016"],"excluded_files":[],"grounding_sha256":"6937df508eedfa38e783092ad97e02b3812b1e0d711005009cfe2b793d1dac0b","head_sha":"39ee810d0a0cf7306f7ccf79dc509f7d6718921a","manifest":"50651f1b5815faafb1dd297f40f4af43c8874a6f5a83e81e99c71694d48e0eda","total_units":16},